abstract: We refine the weighted Fourier-grading argument of OpenAI for average sensitivity
  on the uniform Boolean cube. For every degree-d polynomial threshold function in
  n variables, the note derives AS(f) <= 3.83 d sqrt(n), improving the coefficient
  8 in that argument. The proof is uniform in dimension and degree and uses the positive
  sign convention at zero.
keywords:
- polynomial threshold functions
- average sensitivity
- Boolean functions
- coupling
- Gotsman-Linial conjecture
